position":{"commit_sha":"ea94cdef5fa3903e40ee2f2ea3b0492ed5d090d7","position":"1786100410901037001-8b0ff64c-4d83-4e2b-a532-ea2a968a362d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fae4292fc5817701a1d6f7cdddfc9b4ccd3ccb4fb4a5bcc733bdb86eca7c6cde","event_uuid":"9dc18753-05b9-425b-9d21-8c2c3c6caf1e","position":{"commit_sha":"fe360c862f8067f01fea75c135c23d65f08f9c8d","position":"1786386348639931001-9dc18753-05b9-425b-9d21-8c2c3c6caf1e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9595277e279a728c9d195257e17f48c326aa41cfbdde3ba4a8d75c9115dc8c29","event_uuid":"86905eef-2ce1-469f-9578-a416a2fc2eed","position":{"commit_sha":"85a2c7ce0f6c394713fcb9684ae450a43bd36f7f","position":"1786386374210179001-86905eef-2ce1-469f-9578-a416a2fc2eed"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"16c674d2fa0cdd87083d0c6f890ae5fce7bab55f1c090d61f953692d76a256b8","event_uuid":"2658720f-215b-494e-900a-0e66c6f2705e","position":{"commit_sha":"1ac8c10d3ca537a3df0daf49cba05f79961feb0d","position":"1786386383277847001-2658720f-215b-494e-900a-0e66c6f2705e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6d6a7eef8e42fc6f4038c2707ca9cf7bf555ca29e5673ba814126ad3edf05a0e","event_uuid":"47670865-b60f-4a3c-9875-384acd8504ec","position":{"commit_sha":"b7b946130b0ba1963f4f84ba81c77474dd039f31","position":"1786386385433907001-47670865-b60f-4a3c-9875-384acd8504ec"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"duplicate","comments":[],"created_at":1786100383687978001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8b0ff64c-4d83-4e2b-a532-ea2a968a362d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4bf4-db7d-ce69-45e1"},{"link_uuid":"9dc18753-05b9-425b-9d21-8c2c3c6caf1e","relation":"duplicates","target_id":"6067-fcbd-622b-4c64"}],"description":"## Observation\n\nFound while proving the root cause of bug 4bf4 (jscpd live-clone fixture below the token\nfloor). Not a blocker for 4bf4 — filed so the observation is not lost.\n\n`rebar.metrics.analyzers._jscpd.run_jscpd` reads `statistics.total.{clones,percentage}` and\nreturns them verbatim. When **no file in the scanned tree clears jscpd's `--min-tokens`\nfloor (default 50)**, jscpd 5.0.14 returns:\n\n    {\"clones\": 0, \"percentage\": 0.0, \"sources\": 0, \"lines\": 0, \"tokens\": 0}\n\nThat is byte-identical in the two fields rebar reads to a tree that genuinely has no\nduplication. So `rebar metrics` would report \"0% duplication\" for a tree jscpd never actually\nexamined.\n\n## Why it may matter\n\nThe project already holds the invariant that jscpd failing to answer must surface as\n`Unavailable` rather than zero — see\n`tests/unit/metrics/test_jscpd_dup_heldout.py::test_failed_jscpd_is_unavailable_not_zero`,\nand 4bf4's own AC3: \"a metric that reads 0 when it means 'I cannot tell' is worse than\n`unavailable`\". `sources == 0` is arguably that same case, and is currently reported as a\nconfident zero.\n\n## Why it was NOT fixed under 4bf4\n\nIt needs a judgment call rather than a bugfix, and 4bf4's proven root cause was solely the\ntest fixture. Options:\n\n1. **Treat `sources == 0` as unavailable.** Honest, matches the existing invariant. But it\n   turns a legitimately-tiny or empty tree from \"0% duplication\" into \"unavailable\", which\n   some callers may find noisier. Note `statistics.total.sources` is absent from the minimal\n   report shape used by `tests/unit/metrics/test_jscpd_dup.py::test_parse_statistics_total`,\n   so the check must be `.get(\"sources\")` and fire only on an explicit `0`.\n2. **Leave as-is.** On any real repository at least one file clears a 50-token floor, so\n   `sources > 0` in practice and the ambiguity never materializes.\n3. **Surface `sources` alongside the totals** so callers can decide, without changing the\n   current availability semantics.\n\nNo option is obviously correct without a product view on what the duplication metric should\nsay about a tree too small to measure. Recommend option 1 or 3 if picked up.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A decision is recorded on which of the three options applies.\n- [x] If option 1 or 3: duplication over a tree where no source clears the token floor is\n      distinguishable from genuine zero duplication, with a regression test.\n- [x] `tests/unit/metrics/test_jscpd_dup.py::test_parse_statistics_total` continues to pass\n      unmodified (its report fixture omits `sources`).\n\n## Duplicate resolution evidence\n\nThis ticket duplicates dental-catty-dorado. That closed ticket selected option 1: an explicit statistics.total.sources == 0 result is Unavailable, while a report that omits sources preserves the existing genuine-zero behavior. Merged commit aeb4e036a6ba431e85837acec9d47188f4df0038 contains the exact guard and held-out regression test. Its recorded experiments distinguish an unmeasured tree (sources: 0) from a measured no-duplication tree (sources: 2, clones: 0, percentage: 0.0), and the mutation check reintroduced the ambiguous confident-zero result. Current origin/main contains that commit and behavior.\n","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"2658720f-215b-494e-900a-0e66c6f2705e","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5590-1c13-004c-47e1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"jscpd duplication reports 0% when no source clears the token floor, indistinguishable from genuine zero","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ffab3164-d466-4d2e-8392-71bdeeadbdb9","8b0ff64c-4d83-4e2b-a532-ea2a968a362d","9dc18753-05b9-425b-9d21-8c2c3c6caf1e","86905eef-2ce1-469f-9578-a416a2fc2eed","2658720f-215b-494e-900a-0e66c6f2705e","47670865-b60f-4a3c-9875-384acd8504ec"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659592835070001,"uuid":"1bc4ccfd-1cb0-4188-b698-e8242234327f"}